## Maverick React Component Authoring (MDC Rules)

Purpose: This is the single source of truth for creating production‑ready components for the Maverick React library built on PandaCSS. It unifies our coding style and folder structure, and sets strict rules for API design, accessibility, UX, styling, and Storybook coverage.

- Repo context: monorepo with `@maverick/react` (components) and `@maverick/tokens` (PandaCSS tokens/recipes).
- Tech assumptions: React 19, TypeScript 5, PandaCSS v1, Storybook 9.
- Styling: use PandaCSS recipes/patterns/tokens from `@maverick/tokens`.

### Golden rules
- **Accessibility first**: Every interactive component must be accessible by keyboard and screen readers. Provide correct semantics, labelling, focus states, and ARIA when needed.
- **Consistent API**: Follow the `as` prop pattern, forward refs, and surface HTML props of the base element.
- **Use Panda recipes**: Variants and sizes live in `@maverick/tokens` recipes. Components consume recipes; they do not hardcode styles.
- **Colocation & clarity**: Keep files near their usage, name things clearly, reduce nesting, prefer inline logic, and avoid premature abstraction.

---

## Folder structure & file placement

- New UI components live in: `packages/react/src/components/ComponentName.tsx`
- Stories live next to components: `packages/react/src/components/ComponentName.stories.tsx`
- If a component needs assets (icons, etc.), colocate them in a same‑name folder:
  - `packages/react/src/components/ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx`
  - `packages/react/src/components/ComponentName/asset-name.svg`

Follow the “prefer ≥3 items per folder” and “prefer colocation” guidelines. Do not nest deeper than necessary.

---

## Naming, imports, and style basics

- File name equals the main export: `Button.tsx` exports `Button`.
- Imports order: 1) 3rd‑party, 2) outer modules, 3) same‑module relative imports.
- Do not mutate function args or arrays; prefer native language features over utility libs.
- Prefer descriptive names; avoid implied `get` in function names.
- Initialisms keep consistent case (e.g., `URL`, `appID`).

---

## Component API rules

- Use `forwardRef` and expose the underlying element ref.
- Provide an optional `as?: ElementType` prop for element substitution.
- Extend the intrinsic HTML props for the base element (`React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>`, etc.).
- Pull visual props from the recipe variant types, e.g. `ButtonVariantProps` from `@maverick/tokens/recipes`.
- No business logic in UI components; UI state is allowed when it directly affects visuals/interaction.

Component template (consumption of a Panda recipe):

```tsx
import { ElementType, forwardRef } from 'react';
import { someRecipe } from '@maverick/tokens/recipes';
import type { SomeRecipeVariantProps } from '@maverick/tokens/recipes';

type SomeProps = React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'div'> &
  SomeRecipeVariantProps & { as?: ElementType };

export const SomeComponent = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, SomeProps>(
  ({ className, as: Comp = 'div', ...props }, ref) => {
    return (
      <Comp
        ref={ref}
        {...props}
        className={someRecipe({ /* variant props from props */ })}
      />
    );
  }
);

SomeComponent.displayName = 'SomeComponent';
```

---

## Accessibility & UX checklist (apply per component)

- Keyboard:
  - Tabbable where applicable; `Space`/`Enter` activation for buttons/checkbox/radio.
  - `Escape` handling where appropriate (menus, dialogs).
- Semantics:
  - Use the correct semantic element by default (`button`, `input`, etc.).
  - If using `div` for custom controls, add `role`, `aria-checked/expanded/selected`, and `tabIndex=0` as appropriate. Prefer native controls first.
- Labelling:
  - Associate labels with inputs using `htmlFor`/`id` or `aria-labelledby`/`aria-label`.
  - Ensure visible focus ring (use tokens) and meet color contrast.
- State:
  - Reflect disabled/readonly/invalid via attributes and aria.
  - Avoid duplicating state; sync ARIA and DOM state.
- Announcements:
  - Use `aria-live` only when necessary; keep noise low.

Use `@maverick/tokens/jsx` primitives (e.g., `VisuallyHidden`) when needed for accessible labelling.

---

## Styling with PandaCSS

- Define styles via recipes in `@maverick/tokens` and consume them in components.
- Do not inline literal color values in components; use tokens (e.g., `primary`, `neutral.600`).
- Variants (e.g., `visual`, `size`) come from recipes. Use `variantMap` to drive Storybook controls.

Recipe template (add in `packages/tokens/recipes/<component>.recipe.ts` and export from `packages/tokens/recipes/index.ts`):

```ts
import { defineRecipe } from '@pandacss/dev';

export const checkbox = defineRecipe({
  className: 'checkbox',
  description: 'Styles for the Checkbox component',
  base: {
    display: 'inline-flex',
    alignItems: 'center',
    gap: 'sm',
    _disabled: { opacity: 0.6, cursor: 'not-allowed' },
  },
  variants: {
    size: {
      sm: { '--box-size': '1rem' },
      md: { '--box-size': '1.25rem' },
    },
    visual: {
      default: {},
    },
  },
  defaultVariants: { size: 'md', visual: 'default' },
});
```

Note: When adding new recipes, regenerate Panda artifacts for `@maverick/tokens` per PandaCSS docs so `styled-system` is updated and exported to consumers.

---

## Storybook rules

- Stories colocate with components and export `Meta`/`StoryObj`.
- Add controls for all recipe variant props using `variantMap`.
- Provide at least these stories: Default, Disabled, Sizes, States (hover/focus via pseudo‑class style if demonstrable), and With label/description if applicable.

Story template:

```tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react';
import { Component } from './Component';
import { someRecipe } from '@maverick/tokens/recipes';

const meta: Meta<typeof Component> = {
  title: 'Components/Component',
  component: Component,
  argTypes: {
    // Map controls from variantMap
    // size: { control: { type: 'select' }, options: someRecipe.variantMap.size },
  },
};
export default meta;

type Story = StoryObj<typeof Component>;

export const Default: Story = { args: {} };
```

---

## Example blueprint: Checkbox component

Goal: Mimic native checkbox semantics and behavior, styled with Maverick tokens.

Requirements:
- Render an actual `<input type="checkbox">` for semantics and accessibility.
- Wrap with a clickable label area; support both controlled and uncontrolled usage.
- Expose `checked`, `defaultChecked`, `onChange`, `disabled`, `required`, `name`, `value`.
- Forward ref to the native `input` element (`HTMLInputElement`).
- Support `size` (sm, md) and optional `visual` variant via recipe.
- Keyboard: Space toggles when focused; label click toggles.
- a11y: Proper `id`/`htmlFor`, `aria-checked` mirrors `checked` when needed, visible focus ring.

React template:

```tsx
import { forwardRef, useId } from 'react';
import { checkbox as checkboxRecipe } from '@maverick/tokens/recipes';
import type { CheckboxVariantProps } from '@maverick/tokens/recipes';

type CheckboxProps = Omit<React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'input'>, 'type'> &
  CheckboxVariantProps & {
    label?: React.ReactNode;
    description?: React.ReactNode;
  };

export const Checkbox = forwardRef<HTMLInputElement, CheckboxProps>(
  ({ id, label, description, disabled, className, ...props }, ref) => {
    const autoId = useId();
    const inputId = id ?? autoId;
    const descriptionId = description ? `${inputId}-desc` : undefined;
    return (
      <label className={checkboxRecipe({ /* size/visual props */ })} htmlFor={inputId}>
        <input
          ref={ref}
          id={inputId}
          type="checkbox"
          disabled={disabled}
          aria-describedby={descriptionId}
          {...props}
        />
        <span aria-hidden />
        {label && <span>{label}</span>}
        {description && (
          <span id={descriptionId}>
            {description}
          </span>
        )}
      </label>
    );
  }
);

Checkbox.displayName = 'Checkbox';
```

Story template:

```tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react';
import { Checkbox } from './Checkbox';
import { checkbox as checkboxRecipe } from '@maverick/tokens/recipes';

const meta: Meta<typeof Checkbox> = {
  title: 'Components/Checkbox',
  component: Checkbox,
  argTypes: {
    size: { control: { type: 'select' }, options: checkboxRecipe.variantMap.size },
  },
};
export default meta;

type Story = StoryObj<typeof Checkbox>;

export const Default: Story = {
  args: { label: 'Accept terms', description: 'You can unsubscribe anytime.' },
};

export const Disabled: Story = {
  args: { label: 'Disabled', disabled: true },
};
```

